      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11550847::web::025::worn_surface_morphology",
        "PMC12692809::web::022::3_4_mechanical_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The preformed oxide provides a low-shear, self-lubricating interface.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12692809::web::022::3_4_mechanical_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "A protective oxide barrier can lower wear rate.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11550847::web::025::worn_surface_morphology"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Formation of a dense oxide film can facilitate smoother sliding and stabilize friction.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12692809::web::022::3_4_mechanical_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The adhesion-enhanced film will remain intact during cyclic sliding as temperature, load, and oxygen level vary.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The treatment will significantly reduce both coefficient of friction and wear rate relative to untreated CoCrFeNi from room temperature through 800 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11550847::web::025::worn_surface_morphology",
        "PMC12692809::web::022::3_4_mechanical_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxide film will maintain its integrity under varying loads and environmental conditions.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Conventional untreated CoCrFeNi has minimal native oxide in its standard surface condition.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Untreated CoCrFeNi typically has higher friction and wear because its in-situ oxide layers are unstable or non-optimized.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12692809::web::022::3_4_mechanical_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "High loads and speeds can remove protective oxide layers and expose the substrate to abrasion.",
